<title>GERMANY: AGIV ups stake in Austrian Andritz.</title>
<headline>AGIV ups stake in Austrian Andritz.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial holding company AGIV AG said on Monday it was increasing its stake in the Austrian group Andritz AG from 32.8 percent to 93 percent for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>It said the transaction involved the purchase of the Andritz stake currently held by Austrian bank Creditanstalt.</p>
<p>AGIV said the deal was intended to shift the focus of its holdings towards sectors linked to engineering, electronic and technical services.</p>
<p>It said Andritz made a pre-tax profit of 69 million marks in 1996 on sales of around one billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
